WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.080
At 18, I had about 2,400 bucks to my

00:00:02.240 --> 00:00:06.840
name. At 39, I have a nine-figure net

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:09.200
worth. And honestly, nobody's more

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:10.680
shocked than I am. So, what changed? I

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:11.790
don't have a higher IQ, don't have a

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:11.880
trust fund,

00:00:11.790 --> 00:00:13.600
>> [music]

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:15.480
>> didn't get a huge lucky break. The real

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:17.400
thing that changed is how I think about

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:19.360
money. Many of you are probably closer

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:21.680
to this, and you're wondering what to do

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:23.640
next, but maybe not sure where to start.

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:25.800
This video is for you, because [music]

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:27.560
the difference between these two things,

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:29.000
I'm going to show you. For decades,

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:30.760
scientists believed the human body

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:33.000
physically could not run a mile in under

00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:35.680
4 minutes. Doctors said it could make

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:38.080
your organs fail. Coaches said it's

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:40.080
impossible. Then in 1954, Roger

00:00:38.080 --> 00:00:40.610
Bannister ran it in 3 minutes 59

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:40.960
seconds.

00:00:40.610 --> 00:00:42.320
>> [music]

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:44.880
>> But what happened next is kind of more

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:46.480
shocking. Within 46 days, someone else

00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:48.440
broke it. Within a year, three more

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:49.840
people did. So, basically, it wasn't a

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:52.040
physical limitation, it was

00:00:49.840 --> 00:00:54.040
psychological, just like money. People

00:00:52.040 --> 00:00:55.360
